    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d588">

                <pb facs="0625" n="527" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg527"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.12/44</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">of a Conversation
                        With the Director of the Chinese National Quarantine Service</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Wu Lien-teh</hi>)<anchor n="29" xml:id="d588-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-07-14">July 14, 1930</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Dr. Wu called upon me today at the Country Hospital. He referred to his present
                    position as head of the new national quarantine service and said that he very
                    much desired that there should not be any misunderstanding about the new service
                    which he was organizing. He said that there was need for improvement in the
                    present method of handling quarantine matters and that they intended to
                    institute reforms. He said he had just received a very cordial letter from
                    Surgeon-General Cumming<anchor n="30" xml:id="d588-f2"/> of the U. S. Public
                    Health Service. He gave me the letter to read.<anchor n="31" xml:id="d588-f3"/>
                    In it the Surgeon-General congratulated Dr. Wu Lien-teh upon his assumption of
                    this new work and promised to cooperate with him in every way to make his work a
                    success.</p>
                <p>I told Dr. Wu I hoped that he would not push matters too fast, that everyone had
                    become accustomed to a certain method of handling quarantine matters in China
                    and I hoped that any changes that were to be made would be made slowly.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Trusler
                    Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
